<title>USA: U.S. Treasury permits Cargill exports to N. Korea.</title>
<headline>U.S. Treasury permits Cargill exports to N. Korea.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury has given Cargill Inc. permission to export 500,000 tonnes of food to North Korea in a barter transaction, an administration official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The official, who asked not to be identified, declined to give further details.  </p>
<p>The decision follows an apology by North Korea for an incursion by one of its submarines into South Korean waters in September.</p>
<p>It also has expressed willingness to discuss its nuclear fuel programme and a framework for regional peace talks.</p>
<p>North Korea has been suffering from famine after two consecutive years of serious flooding.</p>
<p>Minneapolis-based Cargill is the world's largest private grain company.</p>
</text>
